## Context
Imported from GitHub issue MinhHaDuong/ImperialDragonHarness#1654 (cross-repo; sen-causal-reading
ticket 0081 exit criterion 2 waits on it). `scripts/zotero.py check-staging` classifies as `absent`
PDFs that Zotero stores identically (same storageHash): `audit_one` (~l. 2249) searches by the PDF's
embedded `/Title` whenever it has >= TITLE_MIN_WORDS words and falls back to `_filename_title(path)`
only when it is shorter; a junk or garbled embedded title (`PII 0304-4076(90)…`, `Microsoft Word - …`,
`ajae_5132.tex`, SIAM headers, `NEO-KEYNBSIAN`) matches no item, no hash is compared, verdict `absent`.
Evidence (issue): `find-work --title "<filename title>" --pdf <file>` → match while check-staging says
absent; with `_pdf_info` neutralised, 12 of 25 such files become `identical`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] When the embedded-title search yields no candidate, audit_one retries with the filename-derived
      title, then compares the hash.
- [ ] Regression test: a PDF whose /Title is junk and whose filename title matches a stored item reads
      `identical`; it fails on today's code.
- [ ] Issue #1654 is closed with a link to the merge; the harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
scripts/zotero.py, tests/test_zotero_import.py (or the check-staging test file)
